00:09:29.383 --> 00:09:32.131
I don't think I ate anything
on my sensitivity list.

00:09:32.131 --> 00:09:33.793
I did eat steak last night,

00:09:33.793 --> 00:09:35.794
which I don't normally eat red meat.

00:09:35.794 --> 00:09:37.274
So maybe that's why,

00:09:37.274 --> 00:09:40.367
but since I couldn't have
chicken, I tried some steak.

00:09:40.367 --> 00:09:42.717
Since I didn't love
that sweet potato toast,

00:09:42.717 --> 00:09:47.125
I'm just going to be having
an avocado with hot sauce.

00:09:47.125 --> 00:09:49.504
- I'm about halfway through
the elimination diet,

00:09:49.504 --> 00:09:52.154
and to be honest, I'm not feeling amazing.

00:09:52.154 --> 00:09:54.466
I don't feel bad, but I don't feel like

00:09:54.466 --> 00:09:55.396
how I thought I would.

00:09:55.396 --> 00:09:57.383
I thought I'd be like jumping
for moon or something.

00:09:57.383 --> 00:09:59.407
- For breakfast today,
I'm having the green juice

00:09:59.407 --> 00:10:00.269
that I prepped.

00:10:00.269 --> 00:10:01.250
Yesterday was good.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.101
I slept really well for
the first time in a while.

00:10:04.101 --> 00:10:05.923
No bloating and goods sleep.

00:10:05.923 --> 00:10:08.070
- All right, it is
lunchtime, and I'm starving.

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.016
And I'm going to treat myself to a BLT,

00:10:10.016 --> 00:10:11.638
and I'm going to serve it
with some basil mayonnaise

00:10:11.638 --> 00:10:12.667
to take it up a notch.

00:10:12.667 --> 00:10:14.631
So the first step is to cook the bacon,

00:10:14.631 --> 00:10:16.893
and I'm going to do that
in a cast iron skillet,

00:10:16.893 --> 00:10:18.023
over medium heat.

00:10:18.023 --> 00:10:19.802
And as you can see, I cut the slices.

00:10:19.802 --> 00:10:21.124
So not only do they cook faster,

00:10:21.124 --> 00:10:22.324
but they'll cook more evenly.

00:10:22.324 --> 00:10:25.114
So now that my bacon is done,
I have removed it from my pan.

00:10:25.114 --> 00:10:27.340
I've taken out some of the bacon drippings

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:28.732
and left a little bit in,

00:10:28.732 --> 00:10:31.311
and then I'm going to toast
my bread in the rest of it.

00:10:31.311 --> 00:10:33.036
Next step is to make some
of that basil mayonnaise

00:10:33.036 --> 00:10:33.869
I was talking about.

00:10:33.869 --> 00:10:35.943
We're going to start with
a little bit of mayonnaise,

00:10:35.943 --> 00:10:37.401
juice of half a lemon,

00:10:37.401 --> 00:10:38.859
all that fresh basil,

00:10:38.859 --> 00:10:41.836
a little Aleppo pepper,
just to spice things up.

00:10:41.836 --> 00:10:43.885
And just a splash of
water to get everything

00:10:43.885 --> 00:10:44.718
going in the blender.

00:10:44.718 --> 00:10:47.193
First I'm gonna spread a generous dollop,

00:10:47.193 --> 00:10:50.373
then I'm going to add some
beautiful tomato slices,

00:10:50.373 --> 00:10:52.954
some lettuce, and then the best part.

00:10:52.954 --> 00:10:54.352
I mean, bacon, hello?

00:10:54.352 --> 00:10:56.062
Let's put that other slice on.

00:10:56.062 --> 00:10:57.064
Oh my God.

00:10:57.064 --> 00:10:57.897
I don't know about you,

00:10:57.897 --> 00:10:59.343
but I think the messier the sandwich is,

00:10:59.343 --> 00:11:00.176
the better it tastes.

00:11:00.176 --> 00:11:02.000
Like, this thing is dripping.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.043
- I'm filming again today at work.

00:11:04.043 --> 00:11:05.538
Betsy, what are we making?

00:11:05.538 --> 00:11:07.985
- [Betsy] Banana bread!

00:11:07.985 --> 00:11:09.875
- [Katie] And I can't eat any of it.

00:11:09.875 --> 00:11:11.567
- Obviously I had to go for a Boba stop.

00:11:11.567 --> 00:11:13.247
I usually get a milk tea,

00:11:13.247 --> 00:11:15.677
but because I can't have
cow's milk right now,

00:11:15.677 --> 00:11:17.437
I went with a fruit slush.

00:11:17.437 --> 00:11:19.230
- I'm out to dinner with
my husband and kids,

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.563
and normally I try to be healthy
and get the turkey burger,

00:11:21.563 --> 00:11:24.382
but tonight I'm going to treat
myself and get the actual

00:11:24.382 --> 00:11:26.540
beef burger because it's
all I can have anyways.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.373
Good morning.

00:11:27.373 --> 00:11:29.519
It is time for another
Kelly car confessional.

00:11:29.519 --> 00:11:32.489
How I'm feeling, honestly, not that great.

00:11:32.489 --> 00:11:34.953
My acid reflux is like
at an all time high.

00:11:34.953 --> 00:11:36.456
I'm waking up super bloated.

00:11:36.456 --> 00:11:37.427
I'm burping.

00:11:37.427 --> 00:11:38.448
It's not cute.

00:11:38.448 --> 00:11:41.537
I'm not used to eating
like red meats and pork.

00:11:41.537 --> 00:11:43.557
I don't know if my body's
in shock and it's like,

00:11:43.557 --> 00:11:45.088
what are you doing to me?

00:11:45.088 --> 00:11:47.099
I think maybe I need to be a
little more conscious about

00:11:47.099 --> 00:11:48.707
just not eating red meat and pork.

00:11:48.707 --> 00:11:51.465
- At this point in the
process, I am pretty surprised.

00:11:51.465 --> 00:11:55.084
I was the only one that was skeptical

00:11:55.084 --> 00:11:56.903
about the food sensitivity test.

00:11:56.903 --> 00:11:58.705
After speaking with Katie and Kelly,

00:11:58.705 --> 00:12:01.487
the food elimination
process seems to be working

00:12:01.487 --> 00:12:02.349
the best for me.

00:12:02.349 --> 00:12:07.349
We are on set today, so we had
to pick our dish from a menu,

00:12:08.268 --> 00:12:10.209
which it's a little harder.

00:12:10.209 --> 00:12:12.365
I got a spicy pork rice bowl,

00:12:12.365 --> 00:12:15.851
and I'm sure that if it's
flavorful, it has garlic in it.

00:12:15.851 --> 00:12:18.212
And that egg roll wrap
definitely has gluten in it.

00:12:18.212 --> 00:12:21.795
Some days you just got
to call your losses.

00:12:23.284 --> 00:12:24.612
- Today, we're all eating together,

00:12:24.612 --> 00:12:26.129
and I'm cheating.

00:12:26.129 --> 00:12:28.755
I'm having chicken banh mi,
and I feel great about it.

00:12:28.755 --> 00:12:29.910
- [Jasmine] Woo!

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.765
- Having work lunch today.

00:12:31.765 --> 00:12:32.664
- No regrets.

00:12:32.664 --> 00:12:33.645
- What'd you do?

00:12:33.645 --> 00:12:34.478
- I'm vlogging.

00:12:34.478 --> 00:12:37.013
- [Katie] I'm vlogging.

00:12:37.013 --> 00:12:38.424
Kelly, are you vlogging?

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:40.162
- Don't look at me, I'm cheating.

00:12:40.162 --> 00:12:41.450
- I'm cheating too.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:42.490
- [Katie] You're both cheating?

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:43.840
- I am not cheating.

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:47.540
I got a steak salad with
everything I can eat on it.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:48.373
- That sucks.

00:12:48.373 --> 00:12:49.479
- It's going to be delicious.

00:12:49.479 --> 00:12:50.312
- [Kelly] For dinner tonight,

00:12:50.312 --> 00:12:52.839
the kids got boxed mac
and cheese and broccoli,

00:12:52.839 --> 00:12:55.227
and to make it an adult meal for myself,

00:12:55.227 --> 00:12:56.780
I'm cooking up some bacon.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:58.097
I'm going to add some mushrooms,

00:12:58.097 --> 00:13:00.225
saute those up in the bacon fat.

00:13:00.225 --> 00:13:02.744
Throw in some spinach
and mix all together.

00:13:02.744 --> 00:13:04.120
This looks pretty good.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:05.389
I already took a bite
'cause I couldn't wait.

00:13:05.389 --> 00:13:06.648
It's so good.

00:13:06.648 --> 00:13:08.214
- I just got home from work,

00:13:08.214 --> 00:13:11.697
and Chris, he's making me stuffed pepper.

00:13:11.697 --> 00:13:14.572
- This no-garlic thing
is driving me insane.

00:13:14.572 --> 00:13:16.141
I didn't know how hard it would be

00:13:16.141 --> 00:13:19.322
to live without garlic,
let me freaking tell you.

00:13:19.322 --> 00:13:20.155
So for dinner today,

00:13:20.155 --> 00:13:23.849
I am having Korean beef patties,
steamed Chinese broccoli,

00:13:23.849 --> 00:13:26.138
topped with some scallion
oil, and of course,

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:27.846
a small bowl of rice.

00:13:27.846 --> 00:13:31.413
I just added tamari, sesame
oil, Korean chili flakes,

00:13:31.413 --> 00:13:33.278
brown sugar, and mirin.

00:13:33.278 --> 00:13:34.527
Mix that all together.

00:13:34.527 --> 00:13:36.593
Then folded in some chopped scallions.

00:13:36.593 --> 00:13:38.892
Pan fried them on a skillet.

00:13:38.892 --> 00:13:39.973
Cheers.

00:13:39.973 --> 00:13:41.296
Tastes like Korean barbecue.

00:13:41.296 --> 00:13:42.733
I do miss the garlic though.

00:13:42.733 --> 00:13:43.853
- Good morning, everyone.

00:13:43.853 --> 00:13:44.686
As you guys know,

00:13:44.686 --> 00:13:46.202
I had that big bowl of pasta last night,

00:13:46.202 --> 00:13:47.853
and I woke up feeling pretty bad.

00:13:47.853 --> 00:13:49.773
My stomach is protruding out.

00:13:49.773 --> 00:13:51.711
I feel bloated, it's cramping.

00:13:51.711 --> 00:13:52.572
I just don't feel great.

00:13:52.572 --> 00:13:54.852
And I know it's because it
was that gluten in the pasta,

00:13:54.852 --> 00:13:57.857
even though the test said
I could have those things,

00:13:57.857 --> 00:14:01.367
my body is having adverse
reactions to these foods,

00:14:01.367 --> 00:14:03.324
and I just know they
don't make me feel well,

00:14:03.324 --> 00:14:04.968
and I know that I
shouldn't be eating them.

00:14:04.968 --> 00:14:07.559
- I am on my last night
of the elimination diet,

00:14:07.559 --> 00:14:11.837
and I'm going to try
some red lentil penne.

00:14:11.837 --> 00:14:14.074
I have never had this pasta before.

00:14:14.074 --> 00:14:16.024
If it's good, that's going
to be pretty exciting.

00:14:16.024 --> 00:14:19.107
The lentil pasta is finished cooking.

00:14:21.736 --> 00:14:22.569
Hmm.

00:14:22.569 --> 00:14:23.456
That's actually pretty good.

00:14:23.456 --> 00:14:25.282
It doesn't have the spring.

00:14:25.282 --> 00:14:27.416
It's al dente, but then as you chew it,

00:14:27.416 --> 00:14:29.315
it kind of crumbles and
breaks up in your mouth.

00:14:29.315 --> 00:14:30.148
It's good.

00:14:30.148 --> 00:14:33.022
But I'm excited that I get to
start incorporating some of my

00:14:33.022 --> 00:14:36.483
favorite foods back in next week.

00:14:36.483 --> 00:14:38.286
- I am re-introducing my food sensitivity,

00:14:38.286 --> 00:14:40.072
starting with gluten.

00:14:40.072 --> 00:14:42.596
I actually don't think it'll
take up to four days for me

00:14:42.596 --> 00:14:43.636
to see a result.

00:14:43.636 --> 00:14:45.265
Because I'm about five bites in,

00:14:45.265 --> 00:14:47.765
and I'm already feeling gassy.

00:14:48.878 --> 00:14:50.393
Cheers!

00:14:50.393 --> 00:14:51.554
I'm happy.

00:14:51.554 --> 00:14:54.416
Whatever happens, this
moment, remember it.

00:14:54.416 --> 00:14:57.087
I had a lot of gluten yesterday.

00:14:57.087 --> 00:14:59.188
I had a whole plate of pasta.

00:14:59.188 --> 00:15:00.956
My eczema started flaring up.

00:15:00.956 --> 00:15:04.846
I was gassy, and I was
sweating a lot in my sleep.

00:15:04.846 --> 00:15:06.182
Like, I got hot flashes.

00:15:06.182 --> 00:15:08.368
- Last night, I had the
salmon for the first time,

00:15:08.368 --> 00:15:10.892
and I woke up at 4:00 AM in the worst pain

00:15:10.892 --> 00:15:12.496
I've felt in a really long time.

00:15:12.496 --> 00:15:13.645
My stomach was cramping.

00:15:13.645 --> 00:15:14.624
It was bloating.

00:15:14.624 --> 00:15:16.390
It almost felt like I had food poisoning.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.940
I think it was just me
having a reaction to salmon.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:20.919
And I really do have a food sensitivity,

00:15:20.919 --> 00:15:24.382
but it really was crazy to
see my body react in that way

00:15:24.382 --> 00:15:26.628
and feel it in a real physical way

00:15:26.628 --> 00:15:28.258
because I really hadn't felt any different

00:15:28.258 --> 00:15:29.459
when I was eliminating.

00:15:29.459 --> 00:15:30.529
Now I get it.

00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:31.362
I get it.

00:15:31.362 --> 00:15:33.732
- Okay, so it's my first
day of re-introducing back

00:15:33.732 --> 00:15:34.992
some of the foods.

00:15:34.992 --> 00:15:36.862
I'm going to start with an egg.

00:15:36.862 --> 00:15:39.551
I cracked an egg, added
some salt and pepper.

00:15:39.551 --> 00:15:40.913
Here we go.

00:15:40.913 --> 00:15:42.073
I love eggs so much.

00:15:42.073 --> 00:15:43.991
I'm going to see how I feel in two days,

00:15:43.991 --> 00:15:46.192
or if anything happens
between now and two days,

00:15:46.192 --> 00:15:48.219
and we'll see if eggs was an issue.

00:15:48.219 --> 00:15:50.184
So it's been two days
since I've had an egg,

00:15:50.184 --> 00:15:52.456
and I feel completely fine.

00:15:52.456 --> 00:15:53.289
I don't know.

00:15:53.289 --> 00:15:56.516
Today, I've added back in coffee,

00:15:56.516 --> 00:15:57.648
and it tastes so good.

00:15:57.648 --> 00:16:00.007
So I'm just going to keep
adding back in these foods

00:16:00.007 --> 00:16:02.915
one by one and just seeing
how I react to them.

00:16:02.915 --> 00:16:05.566
Overall, I have mixed feelings
about doing this test.

00:16:05.566 --> 00:16:09.198
I think removing a lot of my
carbs and a lot of the sugars

00:16:09.198 --> 00:16:11.922
I'm eating and just kind
of the indulgent stuff

00:16:11.922 --> 00:16:13.650
I've been having made me feel better.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:14.669
It gave me more energy,

00:16:14.669 --> 00:16:17.112
but I don't think it
pinpointed to having like

00:16:17.112 --> 00:16:18.840
a food sensitivity necessarily.

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:21.042
- So overall, this is a great process,

00:16:21.042 --> 00:16:23.865
and it's always a journey to
learn more about your own body.

00:16:23.865 --> 00:16:25.566
- It was an interesting week.

00:16:25.566 --> 00:16:26.736
It was an interesting challenge,

00:16:26.736 --> 00:16:31.038
and I'm just glad I got
to do it with my friends.

00:16:31.038 --> 00:16:33.705
- [Jasmine's Boyfriend] Oh, yes!

